  },
  {
   "@id": "http://localhost:8080/cheapest-long-distance-moving-options/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It depends on what you add to the truck. A one-way truck's rate leaves out fuel, motels and days of driving, while a container's price covers the long haul and leaves you the packing and loading. Published figures put each container delivery or pickup trip at $74.99–$150.00. Of the cheapest long distance moving options, total both for your route before you decide."
     },
     "name": "Are moving containers cheaper than a rental truck?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. Other national truck rental companies, such as Penske and Budget, rent one-way trucks, and container and freight-trailer companies offer a self-pack move without the driving. Getting a price from more than one of them is a simple way to find the cheapest long distance moving options for your dates, since one-way rates vary by route and season."
     },
     "name": "Are there alternatives to U-Haul for a one-way move?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "When your load needs two trucks, or the largest size, which is hard work to drive for days. It also loses when fuel, motels, meals and time off work add up to more than a container or a small move with movers. More than 10 items with movers cost $1,650–$4,550 at 1,000 road miles, off peak, so price that against the truck."
     },
     "name": "When is a rental truck not one of the cheapest long distance moving options?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Not always. A broker sells your move and passes it to a mover, while a mover, the carrier, does the work itself. Either way, check the USDOT number of the company that will carry your goods and get its written estimate, so you know who answers for the price."
     },
     "name": "Are long-distance moving companies that aren't brokers cheaper?"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}